# Architecture Rules

## Product unit

The core unit for users is **Issue** (persisted as Event / Signal rows), not raw posts or tweets.
TAKELEY is NOT an X repost product. X is one `SourceProvider` among many.

## Common Intelligence First

```text
Sources → Worker ingest → Pipeline → DB → API personalization → App
```

- User requests MUST NOT call external source APIs or LLMs.
- Worker builds shared intelligence once; many users reuse it.
- API reads DB (+ light personalization) only.

## Backend layers

```text
api (routers) → services → repositories / pipeline / providers
worker/jobs → providers + pipeline → repositories
```

- Routers: HTTP only
- Services: read/personalize/brief for the app
- Pipeline: normalize → dedupe → entities → cluster → analyze → quality gate
- Providers: external fetch adapters only (used by worker, not by API)

## App layers

```text
Flutter screens → API client → Backend /api/v1
Share links → Backend /i/:id (HTML) → optional takeley:// app
Admin → Backend /api/v1/admin/*
```

UI must not embed fetch URLs ad hoc or contain ranking/clustering logic.

## Extensibility

New sources implement `SourceProvider`. New assets/topics extend data — do not hardcode Tesla-only paths outside MVP config.

## Fail fast

Validate at API boundary with Pydantic. Raise clear errors; do not swallow failures silently.
